    description: "Run Cohort 6 of the OptAttest curriculum: VC/DID + Rollup + Governance Integration.\n\nCommands:\n  ./scripts/bakeoff-features cohort --repos ssi,didkit,zksync-era,openzeppelin-contracts,osx,sp1-contract-call\n  ./scripts/bakeoff-features run\n  ./scripts/bakeoff-features diagnose\n\nRepos (6): ssi, didkit, zksync-era, openzeppelin-contracts, osx, sp1-contract-call\nLanguages: Rust (ssi, didkit), Rust+Solidity+TS (zksync-era), Solidity (openzeppelin-contracts, osx), Rust+Solidity (sp1-contract-call)\n\nInitial run results: 2 GOOD (ssi, zksync-era), 4 WARN (didkit, openzeppelin-contracts, osx, sp1-contract-call).\nLLM reflect: 0 USEFUL, 5 PARTIALLY_USEFUL, 1 NOT_USEFUL.\nThis cohort WAS re-validated in the post-fixes sessions (bellman added) with similar results.\nThe \"integration reality check\" cohort — most polyglot, most language diversity.\nSolidity repos have known structural gaps (visibility modifiers, inheritance, 46% orphan in OZ)."  # dae5
